{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-07T10:39:46.737Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"54ac87379db6592d81af1cc6","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1665+pm-gh1666+pm-gh1667","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1665","claim:pm-gh1666","claim:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-gh1667","lineage:pm-9rgaal","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-07T10:39:46.737Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-07T10:39:46.737Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Scope evidence from the pm-gh1665/1666/1667 batch review (Codex round 4, 2026-11-07): the function-and-value signature gate in scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs stops at a named annotation. When an internal module declares type Runner = (options: Hidden) => void and const run: Runner, and an entrypoint re-exports run and Runner but not Hidden, the gate reports missing: [] because Runner itself is exported; the same holds for callable interfaces. That is the transitive type-declaration closure this item owns (the 875 type-declaration references measured above), not a function-signature gap, so it was deferred here rather than fixed in the batch. The fix belongs with the closure policy: when an exported type alias or interface is reached from a public value, walk its declaration (or the checker's resolved call signatures) and apply the same reachability rule, with the per-entrypoint narrow-view decision recorded in the AC.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"e3225635795934317daacccec0f538a8eb415587cddb79c7faf7f174a80bd6c0","after_hash":"2eeef40daea24abdee318d58159acc51cd89e80e6e23c1efe1927d77f550f48b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e176d7608b91478dd43d2716d201d2fd6f62a50b6f7bf344e6766b1f33649917"}
